To implement multi-hop API requests, you can create a function that accepts an array of endpoints and chains the requests using async/await. Here's an example:

```javascript
// src/apiWrapper.js

async function multiHopRequest(endpoints) {
    let result;
    for (const endpoint of endpoints) {
        result = await fetch(endpoint);
        if (!result.ok) throw new Error(`Failed to fetch ${endpoint}`);
        result = await result.json();
    }
    return result;
}

export { multiHopRequest };
```

Ensure to update your tests accordingly in `tests/apiWrapper.test.js` to cover this new functionality.
